e where his father is hanging out  and Viktor goes inside with the gun  while nacho has to sit there and watch  Gus gets inside the car and tells nacho  that he needs to know what Lala  Salamanca is up to where he is going  what he's thinking what he is planning I  need to know what he's going to do  before he does it  nacho has been trying to keep tabs but  Lala has been primarily focused on  burner  mic Gus uses the threat to Papa to get  nacho to try harder and this is classic  Breaking Bad Gus fring this is the guy  who slit Victor's throat in front of  Walt and Jesse and by the end of this  interaction nacho knows his neck is on  the line because Lala doesn't believe  Gus's cover story about the construction  project he goes to visit his tio Hector  at Casa tranquila while he's talking  about Don Eladio and Juan bolsa not  caring about Gus because of the money  that he makes Hector gets his bell  ringing finger and high gear Lalo gets  the message and realizes the only way to  get at Gus is to mess with his money and  get him in trouble with the cartel nacho  and Lalo come together at a poker game  where we see how Domingo who we know as  crazy ate from Breaking Bad got his name  Lalo takes the opportunity to make a big  bluff holding seven deuce on the river  to get Domingo to fold the best hand  before he drags the pot he flips over  his opponents hand to see that he had a  set of eights  as he collects the chips he says Oh Joe  loco this guy and the name Crazy eight  is born while the Salamanca crew was  playing poker are 50% off numbskulls had  arrived at the stash house looking to  score ten bags apparently their spree is  still ongoing and based on the big buy  it appears that things are going their  way the bags got stuck in the drainpipe  on the way down and so now Crazy eight  has to come to the spot and try to  figure out what's going on he gets up on  the ladder to try to fix the pipe right  at the same time the cops roll up on the  location everyone scatters and they all  get away but he's left on the ladder and  has to talk to the police when he gets  down as he's doing that he taps on the  pipe the bags drop out right in front of  them and he gets arrested Lalo and nacho  arrived on the scene to check on the  stash house and this provides an  opportunity for nacho to make a daring  attempt to earn Lala's trust he sneaks  into the house because there's still a  lot of drugs there and he recovers the  stash just before the police bust down  the door well it's a little crazy this  should help move things in the right  direction for him one of the things that  makes Lalo a good character is that he's  no dummy but I really doubt that this  will strike him as a desperate move by  someone who is working against his  interests that seems to be confirmed  later when back at the restaurant Lalo  makes food and has not  to eat with him so that they can discuss  krazy-8 the most exciting thing about  all of this is that Domingo aka krazy-8  is now in custody considering we know he  was a confidential informant for the DEA  and specifically for one Hank Schrader  and the Breaking Bad timeline and that  we also know that Hank will be making  appearance in the next couple of  episodes that table is now set after  watching him fold the best hand in the  poker game Lalo has to be wondering if  he'll be able to hold up under the  pressure of being questioned when not to  ask if he wants him to take care of it  Lalo says no I got something much better  for him this is probably tied to what we  see at the end of the episode so we'll  pick back up with it when we get there  and Jimmy and Kim land things aren't  going very smoothly it feels like Kim is  angry about what happened with her pro  bono client on top of not being fully on  board with a decision to practice law as  Saul Goodman Jimmy's plans to bring  customers in is working but he can also  sense the unease that Kim is having he  tries to improve the situation by taking  her to an open house to give her some  hope about a future they could have  together this seems to work on some  level as she turns the shower on with  him inside getting him all wet that's a  reminder that they do have strong  feelings for each other and enjoy each  other despite the current situation on  the way out she says maybe someday and  it's comforting to see that there are  feelings that a future could be built on  still there earlier at home Kim asked  Jimmy how he was gonna deal with so many  new clients and we see him take things  head-on at the courthouse we see him  wheeling and dealing again with bill  from the DA's office but he's got bigger  things on his mind with a DA Susan  Erickson who you'll remember from Hills  case last season while he's waiting for  her he runs into Howard Hamlin who makes  his first season five appearance and I  must say he's looking a whole lot better  than the last time we saw him Howard  congratulate Jimmy on being reinstated  and mentions that Hamlin Hamlin McGill  is set to have one of their best years  ever he seems genuinely happy to see  Jimmy even if he doesn't really like the  new choice of name and the idea that  things are going so well at HHM is  definitely surprising the big surprise  here though is that Howard asked Jimmy  to have lunch with him we don't get to  find out what it's all about though  because Susanne eggs  the courtroom we learned that she is  assigned to 16 of Jimmy's cases and he  wants to work out some deals to get them  settled quickly  Suzanne see straight through him and  calls him out on wanting quick turnover  so that he can make more money her  instincts he are good and she's not  willing to work out deals with Jimmy  ahead of their scheduled meeting that's  coming up the next week  Jimmy has Saul has gotten himself into  this situation by offering the  discounted rates and this is where he  actually thrives if she won't respond to  his requests then he will concoct a way  to get an audience this plays out in him  setting up for them to get stuck in an  elevator together he finds a maintenance  man who could use some extra cash and  some legal services and when all is said  and done they have come to an agreement  on 13 out of the 16 cases after being  stuck in the elevator together for 20  minutes after he pulls that off things  are looking pretty good for Saul but  little does he know this day is about to  take a turn before we get into that we  have to address Mike's current situation  we catch up with him  at home he's in bed and he looks broth  the phone is ringing next to empty beer  cans and liquor bottles and he's not  moving very quickly to address that it  turns out Stacey is the one who's  calling and she needs him to come over  and watch Kaylee which he agrees to  without question when he arrives things  start off well he goes into full-on  grandpa mode he helps her with the  multiplication tables using the example  of a football game and touchdowns for  sevens and he makes some progress on the  construction of a tree house when the  discussion turns to Kaylee asking  questions about her dad things go  terribly off the rails  we know that Mike's going through a lot  of stuff he's currently dealing with the  remorse over burner and it appears that  thinking about Maddy and what happened  to him after he joined the police force  to be a cop like Mike is sufficient  enough to send him over the edge he  completely loses his cool with his  granddaughter yelling you either do it  right or you don't do it which leads to  her running away to her room when her  mom returns he leaves without explaining  much other than Kaylee was in her room  and wouldn't eat dinner  we know Mike can be a hard person when  he has to be but this was pretty  perplexing and difficult to watch if  there was any question as to how he's  holding up after the events of season 4  I think this clears it up we close out  the  episode with Jimmy who's enjoying an  ice-cream cone after his elevator  encounter with the ad a he's taking  calls and working his magic as nacho  pulls up which I'm guessing is related  to Lalo's plans that he mentioned  earlier it's actually been a long time  since these two have been together way  back in season one with the kettlemans  and the way things were left at that  time Jimmy has no choice but to go along  with nacho here as he does owe him he  gets in the car  unfortunately the ice cream cone can't  come along which is a big loss and they  drive off together and this is sort of  like everything finally coming full  circle  better call Saul is undoubtedly one of  the best television shows that's on  currently but if there's one criticism  that comes up about the show over and  over it's about how the two stories the  one with Jimmy and the one with Mike  kind of exists beside each other rather  than being intertwined that's what makes  this ending so exciting the fact that  Jimmy is going to have to work for nacho  which of course works for Lalo really  moves us firmly into the endgame  remember when we first met Jimmy these  are the two people's names he mentioned  whenever he was being questioned by Walt  and Jesse the show has taken some time  to get there actually more time than  what they had originally planned based  on the fact that Jimmy and choc and that  whole storyline was so good but now we  have finally arrived it's funny on top  of that because Jimmy's deal his 50% off  deal is what set off the spree that  landed those two kids outside of the  stash house that set up Domingo aka  crazy eight getting busted and now he's  bringing jimmy nacho Lalo Gus Mike and  everybody inevitably back together it's  a pretty exciting ending and a pretty  good episode overall we're starting to  see Jimmy hit his stride as being Saul  Goodman we're starting to see the divide  between him and Kim widen a little bit  and we're primed to cross over with  Breaking Bad characters Hank and Gomi  which is going to provide a lot of  fanservice at the same time I like the  one-two punch they delivered here with  these first two episodes releasing them  back-to-back  everything seems to be caught up to  speed  and the table seems to be set I'm  curious to see what Lalo is up to heck  you're telling him to go after the money  is interesting and of course how he's  going to choose to deal with Domingo now  that he's been taken into custody I hope  we don't spend too much time with Mike  being in this dark place that he's at in  this episode with so much other stuff  going on it seems a little bit  superfluous and that we know where  Mike's story goes but I'm not exactly  worried about it because I have a lot of  trust in the writers of this television  show because they are some of the best  in the game let me know in the comments  what you guys thought about this episode  how do you feel about season 5 so far  it's kind of strange because it's hard  to decide whether it's Jimmy or Saul a  lot of times when I'm writing these  things out now he's still somewhere in  between and depending on if he's with  Kim or if he's at work we see a little  bit of both still that brings up the  idea that I've heard Bob Odenkirk say in  a couple of different interviews before  the season started about how Saul is a  persona what we see in Breaking Bad is a  persona I'll be interested to see how  his evolution continues please like this  video if you enjoyed it please leave  comments or questions and let me know  where you think things are going please  subscribe to my channel if you haven't  already I'll be covering this season and  the final one all the way through I may  come up with a couple bonus videos in  between but I'll definitely be doing  weekly recaps at the bare minimum thanks  for watching I'll talk to you soon

